 *    - Only by period (created_after/before)
 *    - By reporting member
 *    - By post ID
 *    - By reason_search
 *    - Use page & limit
 *    - Use sort_key/sort_order
 * 4. For each filter, assert the results returned correspond only to the filter (ids, reasons, date window)
 * 5. As a regular member, confirm that using PATCH for postReports returns an error (permission denied or not allowed)
 * 6. Optionally, test pagination corners: more than limit, exact limit, last page empty
 * 7. Optionally, validate that admin/moderator is not subject to rate limit (e.g. can view all reports regardless of per-member quota enforcement)
 *
 * Notes:
 * - Use random but deterministic UUIDs and ISO dates, but make sure reports have variety.
 * - Assert forbidden for regular member on search/patch.
 * - Check that returned pagination info is accurate.
 * - Validate sort order actually works (asc/desc, by date, by member).
 */
